    (property "LCSC" "" (id 4) (at 414.02 50.8 0)
      (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left) hide)
    )
    (property "Note" "Hardware default-autostart remains POWER_OK & RUN. Former CURRENT_OK input3 is tied directly to this gate V3V3, not fault status; same authentic G11 DBV package. MODEM_EN_ALLOWED drives BOTH MP2386 EN11 and TPS259474LRPWR EN1. PG/FLT must not feed EN or cause automatic latch-clearing. RUN remains external pull-high with MCU open-drain inhibit; main-domain supply loss yields passive EN LOW. Any actual input/rail power loss can rearm the volatile eFuse latch; no AON-retained fault-memory claim. The new compact eFuse PG remains observation/start qualification only; it never drives EN. Blank/reset MCU leaves Q740 gate LOW via R741, so R752 pulls RUN HIGH and hardware starts the modem after main POWER_OK. U16 CT is hardware programmed by R118=100k to guarantee at least180ms protected PG/start qualification before FCPO release; independent OOB open-drain RUN inhibit and MR assertion retain hard-off recovery." (id 5) (at 414.02 50.8 0)
      (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left) hide)
    )
    (property "Manufacturer" "Texas Instruments" (id 6) (at 414.02 50.8 0)
